cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "vf-sim-training: planning simulations for virtual-fence pre-training in cattle"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based planning model of cattle meeting a virtual-fence boundary, with
  group-level Monte Carlo power calculations. It estimates, under explicitly
  stated and unmeasured assumptions, whether pre-training in a virtual
  environment could reduce electric-pulse exposure during the first three days of
  real virtual-fence training, and how many groups such a study would need. It
  is not evidence about animal learning, welfare or transfer.
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/flyapex/Virtual-Fence"
keywords:
  - virtual fencing
  - cattle
  - animal welfare
  - agent-based simulation
  - power analysis
  - study planning
